nos en la masa: cayó en el truco del cine sin darse cuenta. 'To fall for something' significa creerse un engaño, morder el anzuelo. Se usa con trucos, mentiras, estafas y estratagemas de marketing; con personas significa enamorarse.","coach_ejemplo":"I can't believe I fell for that fake discount. — No puedo creer que caí en ese descuento falso.","coach_cierre":"¿Cuál fue la última promoción en la que caíste sin darte cuenta?"},{"expresion":"a rip-off","linea_aprox":20,"coach_intro":"Cuando el precio es un abuso, en inglés no dices solo 'expensive': dices 'a rip-off', un robo. Es informal y trae la indignación incorporada, como bien nota Toby. También funciona como verbo: 'they ripped me off', me estafaron.","coach_ejemplo":"Ten dollars for a small coffee? What a rip-off! — ¿Diez dólares por un café pequeño? ¡Qué robo!","coach_cierre":"¿Qué compra reciente te pareció un verdadero rip-off?"},{"expresion":"to nudge (someone) into (something)","linea_aprox":30,"coach_intro":"Un 'nudge' es un empujoncito con el codo: nadie te obliga, solo te orientan. 'To nudge someone into something' es dirigir suavemente a alguien hacia una decisión, exactamente lo que hace el menú del cine con Toby. Puede ser manipulador o completamente bienintencionado.","coach_ejemplo":"The app nudged me into buying the annual plan. — La app me fue empujando suavemente a comprar el plan anual.","coach_cierre":"¿Qué app o menú crees que te ha empujado suavemente a gastar más?"}],"onda":[1,1,0.95,0.864,0.863,0.832,0.88,0.888,0.96,0.716,1,0.985,0.844,0.863,0.677,0.906,0.826,0.912,0.694,0.881,0.856,0.674,1,0.975,1,1,1,1,0.717,0.793,0.905,0.865,0.726,0.921,0.852,0.961,0.76,0.932,0.876,0.85,0.804,0.876,0.884,0.675,0.865,0.761,0.874,0.824,0.919,0.721,0.813,0.947,0.774,0.936,0.867,0.892,0.81,0.866,0.768,0.793,0.638,0.926,0.831,0.715,0.745,0.862,0.736,0.664,0.784,0.817,0.809,0.838,0.953,0.83,0.863,0.648,0.765,0.675,0.831,0.718,0.909,0.754,0.703,0.956,0.776,0.65,0.828,0.803,0.825,0.741,0.8,0.727,0.676,0.699,0